unty  permit  and they're highly regulated stores that  track seed the fill there's code you  don't open up nearest school the people  going into these dispensaries to  purchase such product has to be of age I  think the sitting Attorney General is an  older gentleman who grew up in a certain  context and we're all victims of her own  context in history so I understand his  position why he has those deep-seated  feelings you know marijuana is a cure  for opiate abuse give me a break  I mean you know this is the kind of  argument that has been made out there  just almost a desperate attempt to  defend the harmlessness of marijuana or  even its benefits I doubt that's true  much of modern science contradicts  sessions dim view of marijuana  therapeutic potential with the National  Academies of Sciences engineering and  medicine finding conclusive evidence  that cannabis is an effective treatment  for chronic pain after surveying 10,000  scientific studies on the matter  nonetheless the federal government  continues to keep marijuana in its most  highly controlled category schedule 1  and recognizes no currently accepted  medical use citing high potential for  abuse with sessions helming the  Department of Justice this  classification seems unlikely to change  anytime soon  meaning the tension between state and  federal law will remain when you look at  it being on Schedule one it's a bit  absurd because the definition of  Schedule one is highly addictive in no  medical uses and cannabis couldn't be  further from the truth on both those  criteria so at the end of the day the  truth is marching forward while  crackdowns on medical cannabis seem  unlikely given Trump's public statements  and overwhelming public support for  medicinal use  what about recreational marijuana after  all that's a distinction Trump's press  secretary Sean Spicer was careful to  make in his comment  the states where it's allowed in  accordance with the appropriations rider  have set forth a pro